    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18272" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flaccus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		etym. dub., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>flabby</i>, <i>hanging down.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auriculae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 9, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of persons, <i>flap-eared</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ecquos deos paetulos esse arbitramur? ecquos
					silos, flaccos, frontones, capitones, quae sunt in nobis?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 1, 29, 80</span></i>
			.—Hence,</div>
